flow "Read repair"
summary "Detects divergent replicas on the read path and writes the latest version back to stale nodes so hot data self-heals."
tags replication anti-entropy consistency
level advanced
source "https://docs.datastax.com/en/cassandra-oss/3.0/cassandra/operations/opsRepairNodesReadRepair.html"
related distributed-systems/quorum-reads-writes distributed-systems/merkle-tree-sync

node client "Client" actor
node coord "Coordinator" service tone=primary
group replicas "Replicas (N=3)"
node r1 "Replica 1" db in=replicas
node r2 "Replica 2" db in=replicas
node r3 "Replica 3" db in=replicas
edge client > coord
edge coord > r1
edge coord > r2
edge coord > r3
array vals "Value@timestamp" keys=r1,r2,r3 = v2@t5 v2@t5 v1@t2

scenario repair "Read path detects and heals stale replica"
  step read-all "Coordinator reads data and digests"
    "R3 missed an earlier write and still holds stale `v1@t2`. On a read, the coordinator fetches full data from R1 and lightweight **hash digests** from R2 and R3 to save bandwidth."
    detail "In Apache Cassandra, the coordinator sends a direct full-data read to the fastest replica (chosen by the dynamic snitch) and digest requests to the remaining replicas required by the read consistency level. At `ONE` or `LOCAL_ONE`, no digest requests are sent and read repair does not run."
    send client > coord "GET k"
    state coord active
    send coord > r1 "GET data"
    send coord > r2 "GET digest" with
    send coord > r3 "GET digest" with
  step detect "Digest mismatch exposes divergence"
    "R1 and R2 match (`v2@t5`), but R3's digest disagrees. The coordinator requests full rows from all replicas to find the newest timestamp."
    send r1 > coord "v2@t5"
    send r2 > coord "hash(v2)" with
    send r3 > coord "hash(v1)!" with
    state r3,vals#r3 warning
    callout coord "Digest mismatch on R3"
  step respond-and-heal "Return latest value and repair R3"
    "The coordinator picks `v2@t5` (highest timestamp), returns it to the client, and sends a repair write `PUT v2@t5` to bring R3 up to date."
    detail "Under Cassandra's default `read_repair = 'BLOCKING'` mode, the coordinator blocks the client response until repair writes reach the read consistency level. Blocking guarantees **monotonic quorum reads**, so a value seen once cannot disappear on the next quorum read even if the original write reached only a minority."
    send coord > client "v2@t5"
    send coord > r3 "repair v2@t5" with
    label vals#r3 "v2@t5"
    state r1,r2,r3,coord,vals success with
    callout r3 "Healed to v2@t5"

scenario cold-data "Unread keys stay divergent without anti-entropy" from=repair/detect
  step never-read "Cold key k-archive is never queried"
    "Read repair only fixes keys that clients actually read. If `k-archive` sits cold for months, R3 silently keeps its stale `v1@t2`."
    state r3 error
    effect r3 shake
    label vals#r3 "v1@t2 (stale)"
    callout r3 "No reads = no read repair"
  step needs-bg "Background anti-entropy is still required"
    "If R1 and R2 later fail or lose disks, stale R3 would resurrect old data. Production stores pair read repair with scheduled **Merkle tree** anti-entropy sweeps."
    focus r3 dim
    callout coord "Pair with background Merkle sync"
